============= CLI >>browse --help<< =============
usage: ncrystal_browse [-h] [-s WORD] [-E] [-f NAME] [-w EXPR] [--props]
                       [--columns KEYS] [--sort KEY] [--reverse] [--json] [-c]
                       [--names] [-x DATANAME] [--plugins] [--color WHEN]
                       [PATTERN ...]

Browse and search the data files available to NCrystal (e.g. files in the
standard data library, in the current directory, or in-memory files),
and the loaded plugins.

By default a list of available files is printed, grouped by the source
delivering them, and with a short description extracted from the header
comments of any NCMAT files. The list can be narrowed down by providing
one or more PATTERNs (case-insensitive substrings of file names, or glob
patterns like "Al*.ncmat"), by requiring certain words to be present in
the file names or NCMAT header comments (--search), or by only showing
files from a given source (--factory). Files can also be selected based
on their physics content with --where (see below), which requires all
candidate files to be loaded.

Files marked "(hidden)" are shadowed by files with the same name from a
higher priority source, and are listed with their full name (like
"stdlib::Al_sg225.ncmat"), which can be used to select them explicitly.

positional arguments:
  PATTERN               Only show files whose names match the pattern.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -s, --search WORD     Only show files which contain WORD in their name or
                        NCMAT header comments (case-insensitive). Can be
                        specified multiple times, in which case all words must
                        be present. Matching comment lines are shown.
  -E, --regex           Interpret search WORDs and PATTERNs as (case-
                        insensitive) Python regular expressions, which match
                        anywhere in the text, with ^ and $ matching at line
                        boundaries (e.g. -E -s "boron|b4c").
  -f, --factory NAME    Only show files delivered by the named factory (e.g.
                        "stdlib" or "virtual").
  -w, --where EXPR      Only show files for which the Python expression EXPR
                        is true, based on physics properties of the loaded
                        material (see below). Can be specified multiple times,
                        in which case all expressions must be true.
  --props               Show the physics properties of each file (i.e. the
                        values available in --where expressions).
  --columns KEYS        Show a table with the given comma-separated physics
                        properties (and "description") of each file, instead
                        of the usual listing.
  --sort KEY            Show a table sorted by KEY, which is "name" or a
                        physics property (which is then also shown). Files
                        without a value are listed last.
  --reverse             Reverse the order of --sort.
  --json                Output all information about the selected files
                        (including physics properties) as JSON.
  -c, --comments        Show full NCMAT header comments of the files.
  --names               Only print the names of the files, one per line
                        (useful for scripting).
  -x, --extract DATANAME
                        Print the full content of DATANAME (e.g. a file name),
                        using the same lookup mechanism as for data in
                        NCrystal cfg-strings. This can therefore also be used
                        to inspect in-memory (or on-demand created) data.
  --plugins             List the currently loaded plugins.
  --color, --colour WHEN
                        Whether to highlight --search hits with colors (like
                        grep): "always", "never", or "auto" (the default, only
                        when printing to a terminal). In "auto" mode the
                        NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR, CLICOLOR_FORCE, and TERM(=dumb)
                        env vars are respected, and the color can be changed
                        via GREP_COLORS (e.g. "mt=01;32"). Like for grep, WHEN
                        must be given as --color=WHEN, and a plain --color
                        means --color=auto.

examples:
  ncrystal_browse                     # list all files
  ncrystal_browse Al                  # files with "al" in the name
  ncrystal_browse "*_sg225*"          # files matching a glob pattern
  ncrystal_browse -s vdos -s togo     # search names and header comments
  ncrystal_browse -E -s "boron|b4c"   # search with regular expression
  ncrystal_browse -c Al_sg225.ncmat   # show header comments of a file
  ncrystal_browse -x Al_sg225.ncmat   # show full content of a file
  ncrystal_browse --plugins           # list loaded plugins
  ncrystal_browse -w "'B' in elements and absxs > 100"
  ncrystal_browse -w "'vdos' in dyninfo" -w "crystal and sg == 225"
  ncrystal_browse --props Al_sg225.ncmat  # show the properties of a file
  ncrystal_browse -w "'B' in elements" --sort absxs --reverse
  ncrystal_browse -f stdlib --columns formula,sg,density

physics properties available in --where expressions (and --props):
  elements       : set of element names, e.g. {"Al","O"}
  atoms          : set of atom labels, including isotopes, e.g. {"D","O"}
  nelements      : number of different elements
  formula        : chemical formula, e.g. "Al2O3"
  mass           : average atomic mass [amu]
  absxs          : absorption cross section per atom at 2200m/s [barn]
  scatxs         : free scattering cross section per atom [barn]
  cohxs          : bound coherent scattering cross section per atom [barn]
  incohxs        : bound incoherent scattering cross section per atom [barn]
  density        : density [g/cm3]
  numdens        : number density [atoms/Aa3]
  temp           : temperature [K]
  state          : state of matter: "solid", "liquid", "gas", or "unknown"
  crystal        : True if crystalline (for multiphase: any phase)
  crystalsystem  : crystal system (e.g. "cubic"), based on the space group
                   (None if not available)
  sg             : space group number (None if not available)
  natoms         : number of atoms in unit cell (None if not available)
  a              : unit cell length a [Aa] (None if not available)
  b              : unit cell length b [Aa] (None if not available)
  c              : unit cell length c [Aa] (None if not available)
  alpha          : unit cell angle alpha [degree] (None if not available)
  beta           : unit cell angle beta [degree] (None if not available)
  gamma          : unit cell angle gamma [degree] (None if not available)
  volume         : unit cell volume [Aa^3] (None if not available)
  braggthreshold : Bragg threshold [Aa], i.e. the longest wavelength with
                   Bragg diffraction (None if not available)
  debyetemps     : dict of per-atom Debye temperatures [K], e.g.
                   {"Al":412.2} (None if not a crystal)
  msds           : dict of per-atom mean-squared-displacements [Aa^2] (None
                   if not a crystal)
  dyninfo        : set of dynamic info types present, among "vdos",
                   "vdosdebye", "scatknl" (a full scattering kernel),
                   "freegas", and "sterile"
  customsections : set of names of @CUSTOM_ sections in NCMAT data
  nphases        : number of phases (1 for single-phase materials)

--where expressions are Python expressions using the properties above,
comparison and boolean operators, set/string/number literals, and the
functions: abs, all, any, len, max, min, round, set, sorted. Expressions
failing due to unavailable (None) values are considered false.

